{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29932 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Picrinine appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the cell line CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence suggests that Picrinine interacts with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like and 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, both of which are targets of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. This compound, in turn, is implicated in targeting CCRF-HSB-2. The shared pathway involves a downstream enzyme that modulates cellular processes, potentially influencing the cell line's behavior. The integration of these targets highlights a possible mechanism by which Picrinine exerts its effects on CCRF-HSB-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
